Strange...

If you apply a figurine, it will ask for a direction. Then, it will say:

"You set the figurine ground beside you and it transforms."

A monster (the monster the figurine is of) will be created. If the 
monster was created hostile, it will additionally say:

"You have a bad feeling about this..."

Whether the monster will be created tame (as a pet), peaceful, or 
hostile depends on the B/C/U status of the figurine. If the figurine is 
blessed, it has an 80% chance of creating a pet, uncursed and cursed 
figurines have 80% chances of creating peaceful and hostile monsters, 
respectively. Otherwise, it will randomly create one of the other two 
hostilities.

There are some special cases. For instance, some monsters can't be 
created tame, such as the Wizard of Yendor, but then again, there are no 
figurines of the Wizard of Yendor.

Note: Statues, however, are not the same as figurines.

